      "id": "inspired-product-s100-p00496",
      "source_en": "discovery, not after. Similarly, it is absolutely critical to ensure that the solution we build will meet the needs of our business—before we take the time and expense to build out that product. Business viability includes financial considerations, marketing (both brand and go-to-market considerations), sales, legal, business development, and senior executives. Few things destroy morale or confidence in the product manager more than finding out k after a product has been built that the product manager did not k understand some essential aspect of the business.",
